<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18822" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">frĭo</span></b> , āvi, ātum,
		1, v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to rub</i>, <i>break</i> or <i>crumble into small pieces</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">terra, quae facile frietur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 1, 9, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">glaebis terrarum saepe friatis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					1, 888</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ut inter se tritum tarde frietur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					12, 19, 42, § 92</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">34, 12, 29,
				§ 117</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ut gemma in micas frietur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					12, 14, 32, § 65</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">friatum amomum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					12, 13, 28, § 49</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
